course: dictionary
lesson: 15100
title: Rudimentary: simple and basic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rudimentary is a word you may meet in history, science and everyday life. It means very simple and basic, and not developed much. «The early farmers used rudimentary tools made of stone.» Stone tools are simple and basic, so rudimentary tools are the first, simplest kind.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «Maya has only rudimentary Spanish: she knows hello and goodbye.» The word only tells you that her Spanish is small and simple, so rudimentary means basic.
explain: In science, rudimentary can mean small and not fully developed. «The ostrich has rudimentary wings that are too small to help it fly.» The wings are there, but they hardly work.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in a simple word such as basic or simple. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Rudimentary means very simple and basic, and not developed much.
fact: Rudimentary can describe tools, shelters, machines, skills or knowledge.
fact: «Rudimentary knowledge» means knowing only the first, simplest parts of something.
fact: In biology, a rudimentary body part is small and not fully developed, and it often has little use.
fact: «Rudimentary» is not the same as «ancient»: ancient means very old, but rudimentary means very simple.
exercise: «The early settlers built a rudimentary shelter from branches and mud.» What does rudimentary mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Made of metal and glass | *Very simple and basic | Very large and grand
exercise: «Maya has only rudimentary Spanish: she knows hello and goodbye.» What does rudimentary mean here? | Very fast | Spoken in a loud voice | Perfect and complete | *Only the first, simplest parts
exercise: «The ostrich has rudimentary wings that are too small to help it fly.» What does rudimentary suggest about the wings? | Longer than its legs | Brightly coloured | *Small and not fully developed | Strong and good for flying fast
test: Which word is closest in meaning to rudimentary? | Ancient | Bright | *Basic | Huge
test: «The bridge was rudimentary, just a plank laid over the stream.» Which clue helps you most? | *Just a plank, which is very simple | The bridge was painted red | Children were playing nearby | Tall trees grew on both sides
exam: Which sentence uses rudimentary correctly? | *The first farmers had rudimentary tools made of stone. | The palace had rudimentary gold fountains and marble halls. | The rudimentary orchestra played a famous symphony in the great hall.
